      "content": "**Zenith Smart Hub Connectivity Issue: A Step-by-Step Guide to Fixing Error 404: Node Not Found**\n\n**Step 1: Restart Your Router (1)** - Simply restart your router to see if it resolves the issue. This is a simple yet effective troubleshooting step that can often resolve connectivity problems.\n\n**Step 2: Check Your Wi-Fi Network Name and Password (2)** - Ensure that your Wi-Fi network name and password are correct. If you've recently changed your network settings, try resetting your router to its factory settings.\n\n**Step 3: Update Your Zenith Smart Hub Firmware (3)** - Check for any firmware updates for your Zenith smart hub and install the latest version. This can resolve connectivity issues and improve overall performance.\n\n**Step 4: Reset Your Zenith Smart Hub (4)** - If the above steps don't work, try resetting your Zenith smart hub to its factory settings. This will erase all your settings, so make sure to write them down before proceeding.\n\n**Step 5: Check for Interference from Other Devices (5)** - Other devices in your home can cause interference with your Wi-Fi signal. Try moving your router to a different location or switching to a different channel",
